Falsifies `subtree_scope::proofs::a_badge_once_bound_is_never_open_again`.

The defect: `unbind` returns a badge to open instead of revoking it, so a revoked client gets the
whole endpoint back.

Expected to fail: the assertion that a badge once bound is never open again.

diff --git a/crates/subtree_scope/src/lib.rs b/crates/subtree_scope/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/subtree_scope/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/subtree_scope/src/lib.rs
@@ -348,7 +348,7 @@
             Binding::SyncOnly => None,
             _ => return Err(Refusal::Refused),
         };
-        self.state[i] = Binding::Revoked;
+        self.state[i] = Binding::Open;
         Ok(held)
     }
 }
